{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TaskLoom"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Cancellation and retries"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/TaskLifetimes","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CombineAndDispatch","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/DebuggingAndTesting","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/ConcurrentWork"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Policy order","anchor":"Policy-order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Modifiers wrap the operation built so far. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".retry(3).timeout(.seconds(5))"},{"text":" gives the whole sequence a five-second timeout. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".timeout(.seconds(5)).retry(3)"},{"text":" gives each attempt its own timeout. The retry count includes the initial attempt and must be positive.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/BackoffStrategy"},{"text":" provides constant, linear, exponential, jittered exponential, and custom delays. Exhausted retries throw ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncOperationError.maxRetriesExceeded"},{"text":", preserving the last error. Cancellation is checked before each attempt and before backoff. Cancellation errors never retry. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retry(_:backoff:when:)"},{"text":" to select eligible failures; rejected errors propagate unchanged.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Cooperative timeouts","anchor":"Cooperative-timeouts"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Timeouts race work against a sleeping child task. The losing child is cancelled, but the task group must wait for every child to exit. A timeout is therefore a cancellation request, not a guarantee that the function returns at a wall-clock deadline. Use cancellation-aware suspension points and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.checkCancellation()"},{"text":" in long-running work.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncTask"},{"text":" expresses timeouts with a default value. It cannot throw ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"text":" to its caller. Converting an operation with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toTask(default:)"},{"text":" also turns all errors, including cancellation, into the supplied default.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Races and fallback","anchor":"Races-and-fallback"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncOperation.race"},{"text":" uses the first completed result, which may be an error. It does not wait for the first success after an earlier failure. Losing child tasks are cancelled cooperatively.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fallback"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recover"},{"text":" propagate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncOperationError.cancelled"},{"text":", and the current task’s cancellation state. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recover"},{"text":" receives ordinary errors so it can select a replacement value. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checkCancellation()"},{"text":" checks immediately before starting its wrapped work; it does not automatically insert checks inside your closure.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allSettled"},{"text":" retains one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"text":" for every input in input order. Individual child failures, including child cancellation errors, become results; cancellation of the parent cancels the group and throws. Choose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all"},{"text":" when an unsuccessful child must fail the overall operation.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Injectable timing","anchor":"Injectable-timing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Timeouts and retries accept ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock:"},{"text":" overloads. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DelayedTask"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RepeatingTask"},{"text":" accept ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Duration"},{"text":" plus ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock:"},{"text":"; their handlers remain on the main actor. A throwing delayed task propagates cancellation. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/DebuggingAndTesting"},{"text":" for deterministic tests.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CancellationAndRetries"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand policy ordering and cooperative cancellation before composing work."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/taskloom\/cancellationandretries"]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/DebuggingAndTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/debuggingandtesting","role":"article","title":"Debugging and testing","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/DebuggingAndTesting","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Name operations, inspect their lifecycle, and advance time explicitly in tests.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/CombineAndDispatch":{"url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/combineanddispatch","role":"article","title":"Combine and Dispatch","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CombineAndDispatch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Use the platform bridges alongside the portable concurrency APIs.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/AsyncTask":{"url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/asynctask","role":"symbol","title":"AsyncTask","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncTask","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncTask","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncTask","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A composable, lazy async task that cannot fail.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom","title":"TaskLoom","abstract":[{"text":"Compose asynchronous work, manage task lifetimes, and bridge Swift concurrency with Combine.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/BackoffStrategy":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/backoffstrategy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BackoffStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/BackoffStrategy","title":"BackoffStrategy","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BackoffStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Defines strategies for calculating delay between retry attempts.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/GettingStarted":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/gettingstarted","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/GettingStarted